## Module structure

- Organize code into coherent feature modules that map to folders in `docs/features/`.
- Keep UI, domain logic, and data access clearly separated as described in `[application-architecture.md](mdc:architecture/application-architecture.md)`.

## Feature documentation

- Each significant feature should have a folder under `docs/features/` following `[template.md](mdc:docs/features/template.md)`.
- Keep `specification.md`, `implementation-notes.md`, and `testing-strategy.md` in sync with the actual implementation.

## Boundaries

- Avoid tight coupling between modules; prefer calling through well-defined interfaces/services.
- Cross-module changes that modify boundaries should be reflected in architecture docs and, if needed, an ADR.

